00:43:33.847 --> 00:43:35.790
"narcissists", it's like,
it's the thing that we all do

00:43:35.790 --> 00:43:38.220
on social media, but there's
a lot of truth in it.

00:43:38.220 --> 00:43:39.830
And I think that...

00:43:43.350 --> 00:43:47.980
it's okay to set a boundary
that is painful to implement

00:43:48.870 --> 00:43:52.200
because sometimes the pain
that you and someone else would

00:43:52.200 --> 00:43:56.250
experience if that boundary
did not exist is even greater.

00:43:56.250 --> 00:43:57.750
But both are painful.

00:43:57.750 --> 00:44:00.690
Like, the boundary being in
place and the boundary not being

00:44:00.690 --> 00:44:02.520
in place are both painful experiences.

00:44:02.520 --> 00:44:06.810
So sometimes there's not a great
solution, and I don't know,

00:44:06.810 --> 00:44:10.140
I mean I think that
conceivably, depending on your

00:44:10.140 --> 00:44:14.130
circumstances and what the proximity is,

00:44:14.130 --> 00:44:15.450
are you in the same town?

00:44:15.450 --> 00:44:17.760
How old are the niece and nephew?

00:44:17.760 --> 00:44:19.530
Is this the kind of thing
