00:44:19.530 --> 00:44:21.410
contact it would lead to...

00:44:22.830 --> 00:44:23.940
Like what would the problems,

00:44:23.940 --> 00:44:24.960
what would the nature of the problems,

00:44:24.960 --> 00:44:26.737
you kinda have to think
about it like that, think,

00:44:26.737 --> 00:44:28.350
"What are the boundaries
that I could set?"

00:44:28.350 --> 00:44:30.750
I don't know, maybe there is
a boundary that you can set

00:44:30.750 --> 00:44:35.220
where it's like, my contact
with my sister is gonna be

00:44:35.220 --> 00:44:38.040
in relation to logistical
things regarding my time

00:44:38.040 --> 00:44:39.630
with her kids.

00:44:39.630 --> 00:44:40.813
I'm not saying that's what
you should do, but I'm-

00:44:40.813 --> 00:44:44.130
Right, but there may be a
creative solution somewhere

00:44:44.130 --> 00:44:45.123
in the middle, and when-

00:44:45.123 --> 00:44:49.260
It's like gerrymandering a new district,

00:44:49.260 --> 00:44:53.640
you have to navigate your
specific situation but draw the

00:44:53.640 --> 00:44:56.460
boundary and communicate the boundary.

00:44:56.460 --> 00:45:00.453
So it's like, when I don't
talk to you about this,

00:45:00.453 --> 00:45:02.849
it's because I'm setting this boundary.

00:45:02.849 --> 00:45:04.938
If you're not okay with that, then

00:45:04.938 --> 00:45:07.740
I'm not gonna have the
boundary here at all, or the

00:45:07.740 --> 00:45:10.320
boundary's gonna be extended
and I'm gonna have to

00:45:10.320 --> 00:45:11.460
push everybody out.

00:45:11.460 --> 00:45:13.980
And sometimes they can move,
so it's not like you're

00:45:13.980 --> 00:45:18.213
making one decision and then that's it.

00:45:19.380 --> 00:45:21.600
So I guess the first
thing we're saying is,

00:45:21.600 --> 00:45:23.490
you don't have to make an
all or nothing decision.

00:45:23.490 --> 00:45:25.560
There's like this whole
spectrum along the way that

00:45:25.560 --> 00:45:28.020
you could make these,
even if it's a convoluted

00:45:28.020 --> 00:45:30.630
type of gerrymandered boundary.

00:45:30.630 --> 00:45:35.630
But then, you know, two days
later or two months later,

00:45:35.790 --> 00:45:38.520
you might discover that
that needs to move.

00:45:38.520 --> 00:45:42.270
It needs to tighten up,
or it could loosen up.

00:45:42.270 --> 00:45:43.430
You know, there's...

00:45:49.035 --> 00:45:53.147
If forgiveness is at play, that, you know,

00:45:54.180 --> 00:45:57.630
it's always something worth considering.

00:45:57.630 --> 00:45:59.013
But it's, you know.

00:46:00.690 --> 00:46:02.080
I think we just have to leave it at that.

00:46:02.080 --> 00:46:03.540
'Cause it also depends on your
personal tolerance, right?

00:46:03.540 --> 00:46:04.590
Right.

00:46:04.590 --> 00:46:07.650
There are some people who
might be in a situation where

00:46:07.650 --> 00:46:11.580
any contact with a person would
be too triggering for them

00:46:11.580 --> 00:46:12.630
where they just can't do it.

00:46:12.630 --> 00:46:15.360
And there might be
situations where it's like,

00:46:15.360 --> 00:46:20.360
this person is difficult,
annoying, whatever,

00:46:21.060 --> 00:46:26.060
an inconvenience, but I'm not
unsafe and I'm not gonna be,

00:46:26.820 --> 00:46:28.950
you know, my mental health
won't be compromised.

00:46:28.950 --> 00:46:32.370
Only you know that in a given situation.

00:46:32.370 --> 00:46:35.640
What your personal level of tolerance is.

00:46:35.640 --> 00:46:37.770
There are people that you can
choose to have in your life

00:46:37.770 --> 00:46:41.400
so long as you know the
reality of what it means.

00:46:41.400 --> 00:46:42.233
Right.

00:46:42.233 --> 00:46:45.000
And you admit that reality to yourself.

00:46:45.000 --> 00:46:48.660
Like finding a trusted
resource, which could be

00:46:48.660 --> 00:46:53.610
a therapist, I think is
a great avenue to pursue

00:46:53.610 --> 00:46:54.450
for something like this.

00:46:54.450 --> 00:46:59.250
A sounding board that you may
have to pay for, you know?

00:46:59.250 --> 00:47:01.200
If you don't have someone in your life.

00:47:02.250 --> 00:47:03.083
Jenna?

00:47:03.083 --> 00:47:07.200
Yeah, I will say I do
have something comparable

00:47:07.200 --> 00:47:11.043
to that in my history with certain family.

00:47:12.210 --> 00:47:16.447
My speaking to, especially,
that you mentioned,

00:47:16.447 --> 00:47:18.360
"she's not right in the
head", so perhaps there's some

00:47:18.360 --> 00:47:21.060
